.\" This manual page is part of msitools.
.TH WIXL 1 "2026-11-04" "msitools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wixl \- build Windows Installer packages from WiX XML
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wixl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wixl
builds a Windows Installer (MSI) package from one or more WiX source
files.  The input uses the WiX v3 schema, with partial compatibility
with the WiX v4 namespace.
.PP
Several input files are loaded in order and share the same preprocessor
variables, include directories and extensions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output =\fIFILE\fR
Write the MSI package to
.IR FILE .
If this option is omitted, the output name is the first input file with
its
.B .wxs
suffix replaced by
.BR .msi .
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-arch =\fIARCH\fR
Set the target processor architecture.  See
.BR ARCHITECTURES
below.  The default is
.BR x86 .
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-define =\fINAME\fR[\fB=\fIVALUE\fR]
Define a preprocessor variable.  If no value is given, the variable is
defined with the value
.BR 1 .
The variable can be referenced as
.BR $(var.\fINAME\fB) .
This option may be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-includedir =\fIDIR\fR
Add
.I DIR
to the list of directories searched by the preprocessor's
.B include
statement.  This option may be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-extdir=\fIDIR\fR
Use
.I DIR
as the directory containing WiX extensions.
.TP
.B \-\-wxidir=\fIDIR\fR
Use
.I DIR
as the directory containing the bundled WiX include files.
.TP
.BR \-E ", " \-\-only\-preproc
Stop after preprocessing and write the resulting XML to standard
output.  No MSI package is created.
.TP
.B \-\-ext=\fIEXTENSION\fR
Enable a WiX extension.  The supported extension is
.BR ui ,
which provides the WixUI dialog sets.  This option may be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print the files being loaded and the package being written.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version number and exit.
.SH ARCHITECTURES
The target architecture is selected with
.BR \-a / \-\-arch
or with the
.B Platform
attribute of the
.B Package
element.  Architecture identifiers are case-insensitive.  If both are
present, they must agree.  They must also agree with the architecture
that
.B $(sys.BUILDARCH)
expands to when the source uses it.
.PP
The accepted identifiers are:
.TP
.BR x86 ", " intel
32-bit x86.  This is the default architecture and uses the
.B Intel
template in the MSI summary information.
.TP
.B x64
64-bit x86.  Components and searches default to the 64-bit view.
.TP
.BR ia64 ", " intel64
64-bit Itanium.  This is a legacy architecture; it uses the
.B x64
summary template and defaults to the 64-bit view.
.TP
.B arm64
64-bit ARM.  Components and searches default to the 64-bit view.
.PP
The 32-bit
.B arm
and
.B msil
identifiers are not supported.  MSI template summary information has no
32-bit ARM or MSIL architecture.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WIXL_DATADIR
Override the compiled-in data directory.  The WiX include and extension
files are looked up below this directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build a package using the default architecture:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
wixl \-o hello.msi hello.wxs
.fi
.RE
.PP
Build an ARM64 package:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
wixl \-a arm64 \-o hello\-arm64.msi hello.wxs
.fi
.RE
.PP
Define a version variable used by the source:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
wixl \-D Version=1.2.3 \-o hello.msi hello.wxs
.fi
.RE
